    "explanation": "Candidate revision 1dbeb0c3163790c35c83505cd1b782a866b98f603bd810c6726449b6646ebe1e passes all six visible public checks on SQLAlchemy 2.0.38, while the original revision failed only test_hybrid_property_and_method_filters with FieldNotFound for the hybrid method `count_square`. The repairs stay inside the allowed package modules and change no public name or signature: models._is_extension_type now also accepts the SQLAlchemy 2.0 HybridExtensionType enum through its name/value attributes and still matches 1.4 symbol values; _get_valid_field_names therefore keeps reporting hybrid properties and methods, and Field.get_sqlalchemy_field keeps calling hybrid-method expressions; get_query_models reads the join compile state defensively via getattr and falls back to _setup_joins/_legacy_setup_joins; auto_join validates a candidate join through getattr(tmp, '_compile_state') instead of assuming that attribute exists, so un-joinable models are still skipped and later surface as BadSpec; Sort.format_for_sqlalchemy prefers nulls_first()/nulls_last() and keeps the legacy nullsfirst()/nullslast() fallback. Exception classes, operator table and pagination metadata logic are untouched. Public checks do not exercise apply_loads restricted-column loading, the documented error paths, the full operator table, or general cross-version equivalence, so those final-acceptance requirements are reported unobserved rather than supported; no counterexample was observed on the exercised paths. Independent frozen acceptance remains outstanding.",
